Third-party work
----------------
* Provider parsing for WeebCentral, MangaPill, MangaKatana, MangaRead (Madara multisrc),
  mgeko (MangaRawClub), ManhwaRead and MangaTown, and the Atsumaru, Hiperdex (Hiper multisrc),
  Omega Scans (HeanCMS multisrc) and Asura Scans API usage (including Asura's Astro prop decoding)
  (CSS selectors, request logic, request pacing), and the
  extension JAR packaging/signing approach in buildSrc/, are adapted from
  keiyoushi/extensions-source (https://github.com/keiyoushi/extensions-source),
  Copyright the Keiyoushi contributors, Apache License 2.0.
* Hentai2Read search form, selectors and image-list format are adapted from the Tachiyomi
  Hentai2Read extension as kept in yuzono/cursed-manga-extensions, Apache License 2.0.
* The Hitomi search (B-tree index lookup) and image-URL logic reimplement the behaviour of
  hitomi.la's public searchlib.js / search.js / common.js; no code is copied.
* The repository index schema follows mihonapp/tachiyomix index/index.proto
  (https://github.com/mihonapp/tachiyomix), Apache License 2.0, including the keiyoushi
  `Resources.jarUrl` (field 501) extension.
* The extension compiles against keiyoushi/extensions-lib (Apache License 2.0); it is a
  compile-only dependency and is not redistributed.

Data and services
-----------------
* MangaBaka (https://mangabaka.org), optional and off by default: it is only contacted when the
  user enables it. MangaBaka-original data is licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0;
  third-party data belongs to its respective providers. Attribution is shown in each series
  description. The API is used unauthenticated within its documented rate limits.
* AniList (https://anilist.co) GraphQL API, optional and off by default, used read-only and
  unauthenticated when enabled.
* MangaDex (https://mangadex.org) public API.
* nhentai (https://nhentai.net) public API v2 and E-Hentai (https://e-hentai.org) gdata API,
  used read-only within their published limits.
Library of Alexandria hosts no content and runs no server; all requests are made from the
user's device.
